 "signature": {
  "says": "The aligned edge. Every boundary between two greys runs at the same sweep, 35° back from the car's length, mirrored left and right, so the whole car reads as one swept wing. Where a boundary has to turn or stop, it never curves: it breaks into sawtooth teeth on the same two angles.",
