 },
 "dna": {
  "says": "Straight lines only, on two angles: the sweep and its mirror, plus the length itself. Sharp corners, never rounded. Shapes are diamonds and swept parallelograms made of those angles. Sawtooth teeth are equal, their sides on the two angles, 12, 4 or 1 cm apart. Line widths 3, 10 and 40 mm. Nothing bolted shows: a seam is a strip of tape.",
